    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "NITI Aayog is an extra-constitutional, non-statutory body created through an executive resolution of the Union Cabinet.",
        "The Vice-Chairperson holds the rank of a Cabinet Minister, while Full-Time Members enjoy the rank of Minister of State.",
        "Part-Time Members are a maximum of 2, drawn from leading universities and research institutes on an ex-officio basis."
      ],
      "id": "bfx5v5v"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Prime Minister of India serves as the Ex-Officio Chairperson of NITI Aayog.",
        "The Governing Council consists of Chief Ministers of all States and UTs with legislatures, along with Lt. Governors of other UTs.",
        "Regional Councils are created to address specific multi-state issues and are chaired by the Prime Minister or a nominee.",
        "The Vice-Chairperson is appointed by the Prime Minister and holds the rank of a Cabinet Minister.",
        "The organizational structure includes Full-time Members, Part-time Members (max 2), Ex-Officio Members (max 4), and a CEO."
      ],
      "id": "4j80hgy"
    }
  ],
